  "name": "atx-v1_1/behavioral-profile-not-object",
  "description": "An ATX v1.1 credential signed with no behavioralProfile, carrying the JSON string \"sha256:ghi789\" as its behavioralProfile, added AFTER signing. JCS(TBS) holds null for a credential with no profile (atx-spec §1.3a.2 rule 1) and otherwise an object of the profile's three members (the credential schema of §1.1), so no signature covers a profile that is not an object. The verifier MUST REJECT with a signature-validation reason. A verifier that projects a profile it cannot decode as null, the absent form, reaches the bytes the signature covers and wrongly ACCEPTs a credential carrying a profile its signature does not cover.",
  "requirement": "§1.3a.2 rule 1: the TBS holds null for a credential with no behavioralProfile and otherwise an object of its three members, so a string added as the profile after signing is a signature failure",
